{%- comment -%}
  Azure Static Web Apps configuration.

  The redirect list is generated from _data/redirects.yml, the same file that
  produces Cloudflare's _redirects, so moving between hosts cannot leave one
  of them stale. Everything else here is Azure-specific and hand-written.

  Harmless on Cloudflare Pages, which ignores it.

  NO AUTH HERE ANY MORE. This file used to carry Entra ID sign-in, a
  `/members/*` role gate and a `rolesSource` pointing at an Azure Function in
  `api/`. That function is deleted: FCPM's identity is passkeys through the
  broker in `worker/`, not a second sign-in belonging to a host we do not
  deploy to. Config describing a login that does not exist is worse than no
  config, because it reads as a working feature.

  What is left is redirects, headers and the 404 fallback, which is all this
  file was ever doing for the site that is actually published.
{%- endcomment -%}
{
  "trailingSlash": "always",

  "routes": [
    {%- for r in site.data.redirects %}
    { "route": "{{ r.from }}", "redirect": "{{ r.to }}", "statusCode": 301 }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
    {%- endfor %}
  ],

  "responseOverrides": {
    "404": { "rewrite": "/404.html" }
  },

  "navigationFallback": {
    "rewrite": "/404.html",
    "exclude": ["/assets/*", "/*.{css,js,png,jpg,jpeg,svg,webp,ico,woff2}"]
  },

  "globalHeaders": {
    "X-Content-Type-Options": "nosniff",
    "Referrer-Policy": "strict-origin-when-cross-origin",
    "Strict-Transport-Security": "max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains"
  },

  "mimeTypes": {
    ".webmanifest": "application/manifest+json"
  }
}
